<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
	A local stand-in for part of what SonarCloud reports, so a sweep can be checked in about
	ten seconds instead of waiting for the scan to come back on the PR.

	Every rule here was verified against the live SonarCloud issue list rather than assumed
	from its description. The check was run at 23ad030, the same revision SonarCloud had last
	analysed, and each rule's findings compared to the Sonar rule it stands in for, file and
	line:

	    Sonar   PMD                                   open   found   caught   missed
	    S3776   CognitiveComplexity                     33      45       33        0
	    S1168   ReturnEmptyCollectionRatherThanNull      3       3        3        0
	    S1488   UnnecessaryLocalBeforeReturn             3       3        3        0
	    S1128   UnnecessaryImport                        2       2        2        0
	    S1066   CollapsibleIfStatements                  2       2        2        0
	    S1068   UnusedPrivateField                       1       1        1        0
	    S1186   UncommentedEmptyMethodBody               1       1        1        0
	    S3626   UnnecessaryReturn                        2       1        1        1

	46 of 47, against 58 findings. So a finding here is right about four times in five, and
	almost nothing Sonar raises for these eight rules gets past it. The 12 extra cognitive
	complexity hits are methods PMD scores above 15 and Sonar does not; they are worth a look
	rather than a fix.

	Two rules were tried and deliberately left out:

	AvoidDuplicateLiterals, for S1192. It cannot be tuned to agree. At minimumLength 5 it
	catches 28 of 29 but reports 185; at 8 it catches 21 and reports 105. Either way the noise
	would bury the 58 findings above, which is the whole value of this file. Add it back
	temporarily when working S1192 specifically, not as a default.

	ExcessiveParameterList, for S107. Its threshold is 10 parameters against Sonar's 7, so it
	found none of the 2 open issues.

	Nothing here covers S135, S1141 or S4144, the next three largest groups. PMD has no
	equivalent, and those need the method read anyway.

	This is report only. It is deliberately not bound to a phase and deliberately not
	pmd:check, because at 79% precision a build failure would sometimes be wrong and a check
	that is sometimes wrong gets ignored. SonarCloud stays the authority on what is an issue.

	Run:  mvn pmd:pmd -Dformat=csv     then read target/pmd.csv
-->
<ruleset name="sonar-overlap"
	xmlns="http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset/2.0.0"
	xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
	xsi:schemaLocation="http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset/2.0.0 https://pmd.sourceforge.io/ruleset_2_0_0.xsd">

	<description>PMD rules verified to track the SonarCloud rules this project still trips</description>

	<!-- S3776, the largest group left and the one that has been finding real bugs. PMD's
	     default reportLevel of 15 is the same threshold Sonar uses, which is why this agrees
	     without tuning. -->
	<rule ref="category/java/design.xml/CognitiveComplexity"/>

	<rule ref="category/java/errorprone.xml/ReturnEmptyCollectionRatherThanNull"/>
	<rule ref="category/java/codestyle.xml/UnnecessaryLocalBeforeReturn"/>
	<rule ref="category/java/codestyle.xml/UnnecessaryImport"/>
	<rule ref="category/java/design.xml/CollapsibleIfStatements"/>
	<rule ref="category/java/bestpractices.xml/UnusedPrivateField"/>
	<rule ref="category/java/documentation.xml/UncommentedEmptyMethodBody"/>

	<!-- S3626. Catches the return case but not the redundant continue in WormholeXTreme. -->
	<rule ref="category/java/codestyle.xml/UnnecessaryReturn"/>
</ruleset>
